I walk into the fitting room with the new shirt.
I want to try it right away.
The cabin is small, but there is a good mirror.
I take off my jacket and my sweater.
Then I put on the blue shirt.
I check the fit in the mirror.
The bigger size is much better.
It does not fit too tightly across the shoulders.
I move my arms a bit.
The shirt is much more comfortable than the other one.
The smaller shirt from Saturday was simply too small.
This shirt fits perfectly.
The length is also exactly right.
The color is still just as nice.
I nod with satisfaction.
I take the shirt off again.
After that, I put on my own clothes.
I take the new shirt with me out of the fitting room.
I definitely want to keep it.
Now I just need to speak with the clerk again.
